# Copy Built APKs to Downloads

Whenever an Android APK is (re)built in this project, immediately copy it to the user's Downloads folder, overwriting the previous copy (never create "(1)" duplicates):

- Technician app: `android/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/HRO-Technician-debug.apk` → `~/Downloads/HRO-Technician-debug.apk`
- Admin app: `android-admin/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/HRO-Admin-debug.apk` → `~/Downloads/HRO-Admin-debug.apk`

```bash
cp -f android/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/HRO-Technician-debug.apk ~/Downloads/
cp -f android-admin/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/HRO-Admin-debug.apk ~/Downloads/
```

Do this automatically after every successful APK build without being asked, and mention in the reply that the fresh APK is in Downloads.

Build notes:
- Gradle needs `JAVA_HOME` set to the Android Studio JBR: `export JAVA_HOME="/Applications/Android Studio.app/Contents/jbr/Contents/Home"`
- Bump `versionCode`/`versionName` in the app's `build.gradle` when shipping a new APK.
